      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TUSCAN ROSE (10) is the one to beat on the strength of her debut second at this track, where she was beaten a neck by Prime Pattern and was near the top of betting. Her latest fifth as a short odds-on favourite on heavy ground was below that level, but she is third-up, race fit and finds a winnable race. BOGEY FREE (1) is the key new runner, a NZ$130,000 Ready to Run buy from the Ciaron Maher stable who has won a Cranbourne trial and brings a nice profile with John Allen booked. CIRCLES OF LIFE (7) also makes appeal on debut after a close third at Camperdown and has Linda Meech aboard for the Wilde yard who go well at home. NORMANDY PEACE (4) has the exposed place form, having worked home for third at this venue when forced wide near the 300m, though he has to prove he can turn that into a sharper 1400m performance.",
